Brighter Pocket Companion names the app it builds Brighter Pocket, and credits Tolkara.

Patch 0021 renamed the Mac app and its links, but its steps, progress lines, errors and
settings still said Tolkara for what the user installs, builds, signs and copies games into,
which the device shows as Brighter Pocket (pocket/patches/0022). Every such text now says
Brighter Pocket: the Install step and its button, the build, sign and connect progress, the
diagnoses, the library, the Play step's notes, the risk acknowledgement and the settings.
Settings > Advanced calls the source folder Brighter Pocket's source, a prepared tree that
tools/prepare.py writes, and the General tab shows the Brighter Pocket version. Tolkara is
named only in a Credit view, on the welcome step and in Settings > General: Brighter Pocket
runs on Tolkara (linked), a compatibility layer like Wine or Proton but for iOS, and is from
Brighter Atlas (linked). Internal names stay: the Tolkara-source resources, the Application
Support folders, the install names looked for on the device, the Swift module and types. Not
upstream: it names this layer and its brand.

